{
  // Tool descriptions for lcp-mcp-interactions
  "describe_server": "Returns an overview of the interactions service and its tools.",
  "list_available_users": "Lists the human users registered in the company along with their roles and knowledge domains.",
  "list_available_roles": "Lists the agent roles defined in the company that can be consulted.",
  "request_user_input": "Pauses the current agent and submits a question to human users in the company. The agent will be automatically resumed once a user replies. Use this when you need information or a decision that only a human can provide. Pass userIds (from list_available_users) to target specific users, or omit to auto-route based on the question.",
  "request_agent_consultation": "Pauses the current agent and dispatches a consultation request to another agent role. The agent will be automatically resumed with the consulting agent's response once it completes. Use this when another role has specialist knowledge needed to proceed. Call list_available_roles first and pass the role's id as roleId — role names are not unique within a company, so the id is required to target the right one.",
  "complete_task": "Marks the current agent task as complete with a final answer. Call this as your last action, after all work is done and any output files have been written. The finalAnswer should be a concise, human-readable summary of what was accomplished. If the task produced output files, list their paths in outputFiles. Each path will be verified to exist in shared storage before the task is marked complete. Omit outputFiles if the task produces no file output."
}
